[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3625816781","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3625816781","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3625816781,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YHZLN","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T09:08:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T09:09:19Z","body":"> The core C++ code does the same thing (not overwriting zero) so this makes sense to me.\r\n\r\nIt does for `Vector2`, but this makes `Vector3` and `Vector4` now work differently for C# and core, not sure that's a good change, I'd say it should be changed in both places if at all\r\n\r\nBut I'd consider this a breaking change in behavior","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3625816781/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626775930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3626775930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3626775930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YLDV6","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T12:47:44Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T12:47:44Z","body":"Note that the behavior of `Vector3/4` is *documented* so changing it is a serious compatibility breakage, as users can reasonably expect this behavior\r\n\r\nAlso the documentation for `Vector2` says it returns `(0, 0)` if the vector has length `0`, probably a copy/paste error but I'd say we should change the code to match the documentation, i.e. make `Vector2` in core behave like `Vector3/4` *and* how it is documented","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626775930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,