url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3627491652","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3627491652,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YNyFE","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T15:28:22Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T15:30:53Z","body":"If there's no change in that sense then the changes should be done to all the cases for uniformity, but that makes sense, but we'd need to evaluate all the specifics to make sure the check is, in fact, redundant\r\n\r\n> and also wasn't in Godot in many places initially\r\n\r\nIt was *always* in these methods\r\n\r\nBut that is a good point and assuming we confirm the behavioral equivalence we'll remove the breaking label\r\n\r\nBut also please keep to a constructive and friendly tone","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627491652/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627550320","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3627550320","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3627550320,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YOAZw","user":{"login":"FyiurAmron","id":11016998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDE2OTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11016998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron","html_url":"https://github.com/FyiurAmron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T15:39:48Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T18:09:12Z","body":"> If there's no change in that sense then the changes should be done to all the cases for uniformity\r\n\r\nOK, I can update the C code as well, no problemo\r\n\r\n>but we'd need to evaluate all the specifics to make sure the check is, in fact, redundant\r\n>assuming we confirm the behavioral equivalence we'll remove the breaking label\r\n\r\nThe only edge case that _already_ exists in code is when you have degenerate vectors, like (eps, eps) that got there by accumulation of rounding errors - however current code _doesn't_ prevent that anyway, and TBH there no \"standard\" consistent way to handle this for vector libraries that I know of, because degenerate vectors are a mostly unsolvable problem anyway.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627550320/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627584653","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3627584653","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3627584653,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YOIyN","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T15:44:20Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T15:45:12Z","body":"Going over the logic it should indeed be irrelevant, it still won't handle cases producing `NaN` as in both cases it'll enter the division branch with a `length_squared` that is `NaN`, so that won't be an issue\r\n\r\nBut if both the C# and C++ cases match this works fine, but it'd be good to have some test cases to confirm it works correctly in general, the code was added in the first place so it should always be verified it isn't actually needed\r\n\r\nI don't remember how C++ handles very tiny values in multiplication so something like `(eps, eps)` might still change in this case if `eps*eps` is `0` and not `eps`, I don't remember if floating point numbers underflow or not, but that'd be the only case changed here after evaluating it in detail\r\n\r\n> I'm trying, please instruct me how to do that better if I'm missing something because I'm honestly doing my best.\r\n\r\nYou removed the comment that had an unfriendly attitude, but please don't vent your frustration at communication confusion when both you and others are part of that communication confusion, but please don't become confrontational because of a communication confusion","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627584653/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627758280","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3627758280","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3627758280,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YOzLI","user":{"login":"FyiurAmron","id":11016998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDE2OTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11016998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron","html_url":"https://github.com/FyiurAmron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T16:09:57Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T16:47:34Z","body":"I've updated C# docs to reflect both the previous and current behaviour (how 0 vectors are handled was not documented there at all), and added C tests for the core case. @AThousandShips I couldn't find tests for C# glue code, do they exist at all? Also, is there some other place that has docs that need updating/making more consistent? ~Current C docs match both the previous and current behaviour AFAIK.~ they don't, they are false for previous V2 and after the change they don't match how the degenerate vectors are handled, because they say e.g.\r\n>Returns [code](0, 0)[/code] if [code]v.length() == 0[/code].\r\n\r\nand for degenerate vectors this might be the case.\r\n\r\nas to other edge cases, I found\r\n>*Note:* This function may return incorrect values if the input vector length is near zero.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627758280/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627889228","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3627889228","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3627889228,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YPTJM","user":{"login":"FyiurAmron","id":11016998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDE2OTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11016998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron","html_url":"https://github.com/FyiurAmron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T16:32:36Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T19:32:56Z","body":">I don't remember how C++ handles very tiny values in multiplication so something like (eps, eps) might still change in this case if eps*eps is 0 and not eps, I don't remember if floating point numbers underflow or not, but that'd be the only case changed here after evaluating it in detail\r\n\r\n@AThousandShips @aaronfranke I finally understand what you guys meant about behavioral change, but I still disagree with the original design (and I think one could argue the change wouldn't be actually breaking, because it would only cover corner cases already mentioned in the docs). I mean, current logic means that a degenerate (near-0) vector normalizes to 0 (with the exception of V2 in C), and that follows from the current documentation (partially, because the docs also allow the result to be invalid, \"near-zero\" is not an exact term). IMO it breaks POLA. C# didn't even document handling those cases at all, but indeed C did, and indeed if consistency is to be achieved, those would need to match. Currently V2 in C doesn't follow the documentation and implementation of other cases and C# documentation is broken because it says that normalization is strictly equal to /= len, while it isn't for 0-length (0 and degenerate) vectors.\r\n\r\nThe main problem I see is that there's a difference between the docs mentioning **both** \"length\" (which is a mathematical concept) and \"length()\" which is the result of actual function call. Those are not strictly equal - length is 0 only if all components are zero, and length() is zero if all components are strictly below sqrt(float.MIN_VALUE) (a lot lower than eps, but still). This is confusing, and I think the proper way to handle it would be to just use the mathematical term exclusively.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627889228/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3630465664","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113716#issuecomment-3630465664","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113716","id":3630465664,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YZIKA","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-09T05:52:39Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T05:54:15Z","body":"Also see #74983 and #74912 which fixes this and other problems, like non-unit length results, and provides a function which returns failure.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3630465664/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]